<title>TUNISIA: Libya says will send food to Iraq.</title>
<headline>Libya says will send food to Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libya will send food to Iraq ahead of the Islamic fasting month of Ramadan, the official Libyan news agency JANA reported on Friday.</p>
<p>JANA, received in Tunis, said Libya would send &quot;big&quot; amounts of aid did not give details. It said Libya appealed to all Arab states to follow its example and send aid to Iraq. Ramadan starts around January 10.</p>
<p>Iraq this week accepted United Nations conditions to sell $2 billion of oil in a six-month period to buy food and medicine. But Baghdad remains under a U.N. trade embargo imposed since its invasion of Kuwait in 1990.</p>
